**Kummer's Transformation of Series**

#### 3.6.26 Let \(\mathop{\sum}_{k=0}^{\infty}a_{k}=s\) be a given convergent series and

\(\sum\limits_{k=0}^{\infty}c_{k}=c\) be a given convergent series with known sum \(c\) such that \(\lim\limits_{k\rightarrow\infty}\frac{a_{k}}{c_{k}}=\lambda\neq 0\). Then

\(s=\lambda c+\mathop{\sum}_{k=0}^{\infty}\left(1-\lambda\,\frac{c_{i}}{a_{k}} \right)a_{k}\).

**Euler's Transformation of Series**

6.27 If \(\mathop{\sum}_{k=0}^{\infty}\;(-1)^{st}a_{k}=a_{0}-a_{1}+a_{2}-\) . . . is a convergent series with sum \(s\) then

\(s=\mathop{\sum}_{k=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{st}\lambda a_{k}}{2^{s+1}}\,\Delta^{ st}a_{0}=\mathop{\sum}_{n=0}^{\xi}\;(-1)^{st}\left(\begin{array}{l}k\\ m\end{array}\right)a_{k-m}\)

